  "answer_text": "Despite his name, Flounder from *The Little Mermaid* is **not actually a flounder**. Real-life flounders are flat, brown bottom-feeders with both of their eyes on one side of their head\u2014not at all like the chubby, bright yellow-and-blue character from the movie!\n\nInstead, Flounder's design is based on other tropical reef fish:\n\n* **The Live-Action Remake (2023):** In the live-action movie, Flounder's species was officially confirmed by Disney to be a **sergeant major** (a type of damselfish). Real-life sergeant majors (*Abudefduf saxatilis*) are oval-shaped tropical fish with bright yellow backs and blue-to-black vertical stripes, which matches Flounder's coloring. \n* **The Animated Movie (1989):** In the original cartoon, Flounder's design is a bit more stylized and cartoonish. While his vertical stripes and round shape always resembled a sergeant major, animators and fans also noted similarities to other colorful reef fish, such as a **blue angelfish** or other tropical damselfish.",
